sequenceDiagram

%% config
autonumber
participant controller as controller : GameController
participant computer as computer : ComputerPlayer
participant strategy as strategy : WinningThenRandomStrategy
participant game as game : GomokuGame
participant board as board : Board
participant history as history : MoveHistory

%% steps
Note over controller,game: Computer is Player 2 and a legal O move is available that completes five in a row.
controller->>controller: MakeCurrentPlayerMove()
controller->>computer: ChooseMove(game)
computer->>strategy: ChooseMove(game, computer)
strategy->>game: GetValidMoves()

loop Cell candidates until an immediate win is found
    strategy->>game: WouldMoveWin(candidate)
    game->>game: HasWinningLine(row, column, symbol)
    game-->>strategy: true or false
end
strategy-->>computer: winningMove
computer-->>controller: winningMove

controller->>game: MakeMove(winningMove)
game->>board: PlaceMove(winningMove)
game->>computer: UsePiece(winningMove.GetPiece())
Note over computer: Reusable O mark remains available throughout.

game->>history: AddMove(winningMove)
game->>game: EvaluateResult()
Note over game: Result = PLAYER_TWO_WIN. No player switch due to win.
game-->>controller: true

Note over controller: On the next Run tick, these methods print the board/result
controller->>controller: DisplayGame()
controller->>controller: DisplayResult()